  "schema": "voltmarkt",
  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_pat",
  "prompt": "Which categories lost volume after February's price rises? For each category (products.category_id) with a price rise that took effect from 1 to 28 February 2025, add up the units of all its rises over their before windows and over their after windows, and give the percentage change: 100 times (units after minus units before) divided by units before, rounded to 1 decimal with ROUND; a category with no units before shows a missing change. A price rise is a version in price_history whose list_price_eur is higher than that of the product's version before it, dated by its valid_from. Its change week is the week (Monday to Sunday) that holds valid_from. The before window is the 8 weeks just before the change week and the after window the 8 weeks just after it; the change week itself is in neither. Units come from weekly_units, which has a row for every product and week (week_start is the Monday), with 0 for a week with no sale. Leave out a rise of a product whose launch_date is later than the first day of its before window (the Monday 8 weeks before the change week). Return five columns, in this order: category_id, rises (the number of rises that stay), units_before, units_after and pct_change. Return one row per category with a rise that stays. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "category_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "rises",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "units_before",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "units_after",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
